256 pieces of half-type data. Core 0 implements the x+y operation and stores the
result in the first half of z. Core 1 stores the computation result of core 0 in x,
adds the computation result to y, and stores the result in the second half of z.
Therefore, data synchronization needs to be performed between multiple cores.
